title: memfs file watching
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

This is a standalone example of connecting memfs file watching to Notebook Kit reactivity. observeMemfs follows the same Generators.observe pattern as [[observeTwFilter]]: it publishes the initial ready state, forwards each fs.watch callback, and closes the watcher when Notebook Kit disposes the cell.

The automatic write cell writes one file only after the watcher publishes its initial ready value. The buttons below then create a random file or append a dated line to notes.txt. Watcher events refresh the directory listing, but never trigger either write cell, preventing a feedback loop. For a Git repository, watch a user-facing directory or individual file rather than the whole repository: Git writes many files below .git.

